        <summary>Gets the setting that displays an alphabetic ISO 4217 currency code instead of a currency symbol.</summary>
        <value>The currency-width setting that displays a three-letter code, such as USD.</value>
        <remarks>
          <para>This setting uses the currency's alphabetic code, not its numeric ISO code. Its behavior for units other than currencies is unspecified.</para>
          <para>The <format type="text/html"><a href="https://github.com/unicode-org/icu/blob/ba177f104da42d8a44b20d59e99d0c4b0073c789/icu4j/main/core/src/main/java/com/ibm/icu/impl/number/MutablePatternModifier.java#L411-L417">ICU currency-symbol implementation</a></format> selects <c>Currency.getCurrencyCode()</c> for this option.</para>
        </remarks>
      </Docs>
    </Member>
